        {
          "Key": "Padding",
          "Method": "MapPadding",
          "Status": "NoOp",
          "Reason": "Intentional no-op, carried over from dotnet/maui. The platform view is a \u003Cc\u003ETizen.UIExtensions.NUI.Image\u003C/c\u003E, i.e. a NUI \u003Cc\u003EImageView\u003C/c\u003E. content-inset API\u0022 was imprecise. It is nonetheless the wrong tool: NUI padding insets a view\u0027s \u003Cem\u003Echildren\u003C/em\u003E during layout, and an \u003Cc\u003EImageView\u003C/c\u003E renders its image as a visual rather than as a child, so writing padding would move nothing while making the view report a larger measured size. Insetting the image itself would mean wrapping it in a container view, which this backend cannot do: MAUI exposes no settable container hook to an out-of-repo assembly, so \u003Cc\u003ETizenViewHandler\u003C/c\u003E pins \u003Cc\u003ENeedsContainer\u003C/c\u003E to false. Recorded as a gap rather than faked. Not verified on a device \u2014 see docs/net11-status.md."
        }
      ],
